WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.860
Want to get rid of the president? Awesome.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.020
First, find an impeachable offense:

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.340
What's an impeachable offense?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.860
Treason, Bribery or "Other High Crimes and
Misdemeanors."

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.780
Okay, so what's "other high crimes and misdemeanors?"

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.440
Nobody knows.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.079
Some people say it means bad things only people
in high office can do -

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.400
like misusing public assets or dereliction
of duty

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.680
or getting a hummer under the Resolute Desk.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.260
Others say it doesn’t mean minor, everyday
criminal behavior —

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.880
just really bad criminal behavior,

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.800
like lying under oath about getting a hummer
under the Resolute desk.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.780
Others say it's any crime or misdemeanor at all,

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.900
even if it has nothing to do with their their position of power.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.200
Did you steal that pen from work?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.349
Petty theft is a misdemeanor.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:32.469
You are no longer President.

00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:35.160
Government officials have been impeached for
submitting false expense reports,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.320
lying under oath, even showing up to work drunk.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.300
It's a pretty wide net.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.000
Of course, this is the highest office in the
land we're talking about,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.580
and considering all the shit presidents have
done without being impeached,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.600
it's a pretty high bar.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.660
So to sum up: it's a wide net, with a high
bar.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.880
So once you get an impeachable offense,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.800
get a majority of the house to vote for it
and then go to trial in the Senate --

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.170
call witnesses, present evidence --

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.400
it's pretty much like a normal court case,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.520
except the judge is the chief justice of the supreme court,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.380
the prosecuting attorneys are members of the
House,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.280
and it takes place in the freaking Senate.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.179
Then after a couple of months of the highest
rated programming in CSPAN history,

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.340
the senators vote -- and if 67 senators find
the President guilty, he's gone.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.600
But what if there was another way?

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.840
Without all that messy law and order stuff?

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.120
The Vice President and a majority of the cabinet
can invoke the 25th amendment

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.890
and present a written declaration to Congress

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.980
that the President is "unable to discharge
the powers and duties of his office,"

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:19.980
Okay, what does that mean?

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.590
Well, in the past it's been used for things
like "Hey, I'm getting a colonoscopy,

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.010
can you cover for me for a few hours?"

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.680
but now some people want it to mean "I just
think this guy is an asshat."

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.880
Regardless of the rationale, once those articles
are invoked, the magic wand is waved

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.880
and the President is immediately stripped
of power.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.960
No trial, no witnesses, no evidence, no votes
-- just gone.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.500
Of course the President is going to say "Hey,
I'm totally fit for office,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.400
get out of my chair"

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.040
but if the Vice President won't budge, then
it goes back to congress,

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.610
which will have three weeks to decide who
gets to run things.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.321
This time though you need 2/3rds of the Senate
and 2/3rds of the House

00:01:46.321 --> 00:01:48.500
or maybe it's 2/3rds of the Senate and the
House,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.560
nobody really knows because it's never happened
before

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.810
and it'll probably end up going to the Supreme
Court anyway.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.720
Regardless, if enough of them agree that the
President is an asshat or whatever,

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.220
the Vice President stays put,
and the President is never heard from again.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.000
Or more likely he goes on twitter

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.940
and says this was an extra-judicial coup by Washington insiders

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.500
and starts a new civil war, only this time
with bigger guns

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.120
and planes and bombs and stuff.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.260
So maybe we shouldn't decide to get rid of
a President just because we hate them

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:14.300
and then, afterwards, figure out how to pretend
it's the law.

